DRIP project (Data Retrieval and Ingestion Platform)

------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------


About:
    this is like a notes app which helps with providing you an user interface, where you can write some notes in a specific format and then let the platform pick up a spot in your knowledge base to store that information.
    you just have to specify a knowledge base folder which acts as a knowledge tree for your retrieval and ingestion/storage

Working of this DRIP Application: 
    - tech stack
    - main components 
        - Knowledge Base
        - Platform
        - Ingestion
        - Retrieval 


Tech Stack:
    - explored the widely used programming languages that are widely used in code editors and text editors and seen how performance and developability factor in this space and how electron outweights some traditional c++ most efficient platforms as electron has easy usability and can really help with faster developement
    - seen the various architectures to build this platform, seen other already implemneted solutions like obsidian, vscode. which doesn't make use of a database but only rely on the existing folder structure which is used as a database.. and I have also learnt an intersting thing about the differences between electron(desktop-web-app) and a standard web interface which makes uses of system folder structure from the browser. why electron like desktop-web apps are prefered to web interface to access the system folder strucrtures, because browsers are not permited to have complete access to system files.. and electron has many such 
    - got to conclude it is better if we can clone the open source code of vscode and understand the working of it and get to konw the basics of electron and its specific features and components and API which are specific to it..
    - start working on this open source code as a base foundation, remove all the unnecessary parts which are not required now and keep the folder structure as simple as possible and modify the code as required.. to implemnted the features that you want to design
