Main Components:

    1. Knowledge Base:
        - Talks about the database structure i.e the database folder structure
        - the main knowledge base folder has a specific folder structure that the project follows:
            - each folder/ sub-folders
                - has a .dripignore file that has a list of all the files which are not to be included in the platform's knowledge base/tracked by it
                - has a index.json file that has the metadata like: 
                    tags (indicating it as a project/concept folder)
                    list of all the file names and sub-folders present in that specific folder
                    linear/chronological hierarchy of the current files if there are any present
                        linear hierarchy -> this helps when you have split the file into 2 files and you have a first and second part just broken based on the amount of content/ topic wise sections where you can say part 1 is the pre-req of part 2
                        chronological hierarchy -> this helps when you have split the file and you have some time dependent learnings of how a particular problem was implemented a while ago and how it is utilized now in modern times.. 
            - each file 
                - follows a strict markdown format so that it becomes easier to parse when you want to do some modifications to the file from the application platform
                - has metadata in the header which is parsable by the platform, this includes
                    about: a brief explanation of what is in this file
                    index: list of all the contents present    
        - metadata 
            - for folders in index.json
            - for files at the header
            - metadata includes
                - tags: 
                - priority:
                - timestamp:
                - modified: 
