    3. Ingestion:
        - selecting the Note Template
            - you have a list of different types of notes to choose from and you select one of these note types 
            - you can add these different note types as extensions of the common note interface
            - each note type is designed individually according to the user needs
            - note types 
                - question answering
                - short concept 
                - long concept 
                - project type 
                - research oriented 
        - filling the note template with the data what you have in mind/ what you have learned about 
            - maybe you can have a rough notes written in a paragraph format and an ai model API can be used here to make this paragraph into a proper structured format by a custom prompt given by you. 
        - in the training phase/ when you have time to look at where exactly is this note placed, you will go through the entire below process 
            or the retriever selects a suitable place and places your newly created note there in a simple manner without any complication/ training
        - searching the entire knowledge base to find the closest folder/ file name to keep this note in 
            - create a new file under the referenced folder name 
            - create a new section under an existing referenced file 
        - note: this only checks the .md files in the folders of your knowledge base but don't touch any code files present or any .txt files present 
        - platform gives you the top 10 choices of the file names/ folder names 
            - you have to choose from these options 
            - if nothing within a specific score range got retrieved by the retriever you will make a new file from a given list of folder names 
        - Extracting the data --> each of your choice gets saved in a training data format to train the Retriever AI
        - from the choice of the file, you will get the required markdown tree of the file structure 
            - choice of top 5 positions to choose from  
            - choices to choose from 
                - create a new section/ sub section
                - add the note to an existing section 


    4. Retrieval:
        - you go to the retrieval tab 
        - you give a query => converts the query into an embedding
        - searches the entire knowledge base
        - get the top 10 closest nodes(folder/file names) closest to the query 
        - folders -> get files 
        - files -> get sections/ sub-sections 
        - collecting the training data to train the ai when you have time/ when your application is in the training phase 
            - explore each file/section among the given choices and give rating which is the closest to update the AI 
        - note: Implementing an Algorithm to retireve these similar nodes to the query, in the knowledge base is soo hard 
        distance between the query and the nodes must be the least 
    

