Software Design Principles
    - functionality that you want this application to follow
        - the data must be portable if you want to move it up to another platform, i.e. the parsing logic must be soo good and it has to be perfect to be used by another platform if it wants to extract the data from these files
        - you must have the ability to instantiate different folders within the main folder with this DRIP framework and the application must not fail or break any where if you made changes to these specific project files externally outside the framework
        - you must have a .dripignore file to ignore any files or folders so that you only work with a little subset of the entire folder structure of the project instead of working with all the files/folders present in the project which might make it more complex.. you use this just for the ingestion/retireval tabs but not for the activity/tasks/questions tab as they should have a whole picture rather than looking into individual paths, but you can have filters to just filter out only those activities with the sub folder which is selected.. 
