Phase - II 
    - Updated features compared to phase I 
    - Implementing design choices for the below 
        - do we have to consider the folder/ file names to be representive of the content in them with each addition of new content/notes to them?? 
        - do the folders have mutually exclusive files in them so that no files in the folder can have similar kind of content or can them like interconnect with each other?? which is a good design principle 
            - this destroys connectivity/graph structures between the files but can get good retrieval properties as a specific content can only be found in a specific region without any connections with the other files 
            - but this is a tradeoff so you have to find balance between them both.. 
        - finding the right balance and seeing what the tradeoff is between a human organization of the folderstructure and letting the ai completely take over this structure and file/folder names 
    - shortening the file/folder 
        - when there are too many files in a folder --> spliting the folder and creating a new folder
        - when there are too many sections in a file --> create a new file and split the contents of the old file 
        - what is the best methodology to implement this feature??
        - is it like a clean button that we run once in a while to make sure that the optimal structure is maintained in the knowledge base so that all the files are well balanced and not too heavy at some parts 
    - shorten function algorithm
        - to shorten files/folders and split some heavy content into 2 or more parts 
        - include code for agentic AI to suggest suitable names to do a split
    - how to deal with files with code scripts inside them and how to extend this application to act like a knowledge base even for learning code bases... 
    - support for images in marddown?? 
    - updating the retrieval/embedding model & finetuning it better 
